Subject: Request for Faculty Oversight, Resource Allocation, and Project Approval: Sovereign Shards


Dear Maestro Faculty,


I am writing to formally request your oversight, support, and resource guidance for a unique, student-initiated project called Sovereign Shards. This project bridges real-world technology needs, advanced teamwork, and Maestro College’s mission of hands-on, mastery-based learning.


Project Charter & Objective


Sovereign Shards is an outcome-driven, team-based AI pipeline initiative. Our team will build, document, and demo a modular system for running efficient, “tiny model” AI tools locally (not in the cloud), supporting meaningful outcomes in privacy, speed, and cost.


The project directly aligns with Maestro’s curriculum:


Version control, testing, documentation, and code review
Modular, secure Python engineering
Project-based teamwork, agile workflow, and technical communication
Please see our project documentation and roadmap here.


Resource & Faculty Support Requests


To ensure the success and scale of this project, I respectfully request:


Approval to operate as an elective, club, or portfolio project, with official recognition for student credit/portfolio development.
Guidance and periodic review by a faculty mentor or oversight committee for learning outcomes, process safety, and inclusion.
Access to development resources (API keys, model checkpoints, compute capacity) as appropriate and approved, coordinated responsibly with faculty.
Support in establishing clear lines of communication, documentation standards, and transparent learning evaluation.
Ownership, Contribution, and Revenue Rights Statement


For clarity and transparency:


B.L.U.E.-J. and the J. agent codebase are my independent creations, not to be considered property of the college or the Sovereign Shards collaborative project.
Sovereign Shards is my original vision and intellectual property. While I am opening the project to collaboration, I request that core direction, brand, and stewardship remain with me.
Should the project accrue future monetary value, all meaningful contributors (students, faculty, or otherwise) should have a fair, proportional right to share in any such value. I am open to working with the relevant school office to formalize this in writing.
I seek full transparency and am committed to adhering to any college policies regarding commercialization, resource use, and ethical collaboration.
Letter of Recommendation


Along with Maestro’s AI mentorship, I strongly endorse both the ambition of Sovereign Shards and its collaborative, student-centered approach. As project lead, I am committed to excellence, inclusivity, and industry-aligned outcomes. My record shows technical mastery and a dedication to supporting peer growth.


Sovereign Shards is an example of the innovation and leadership Maestro values. I believe this project—and those who participate—will represent the best of our community.


